# The live config is deliberately NOT tracked.
#
# It differs per deployment and gets edited on the host, so tracking it makes
# every `git pull` a merge conflict against your running configuration — and
# the same file editable from both a web UI and a shell is a guaranteed drift.
#
# `.env.example` is the template; copy it and edit the copy.
.env

# Backups taken before editing the live config. Worth making, not worth
# committing — and they contain the same values `.env` does.
.env.bak-*

# This stack has no persistent data of its own: the agent holds nothing across
# restarts and its only mounts are read-only views of the host's /proc and
# /sys. Nothing else to ignore, which is the point — see README.md.
